1
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:02,540
The ride never came.

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:06,260
The clinic closed before her shift ended.

3
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:09,780
The form asked for papers she didn't have.

4
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:13,540
The next appointment was six weeks away.

5
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:17,313
Each one is a barrier on the way to care.

6
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:19,903
And most of them are never counted.

7
00:00:21,143 --> 00:00:25,243
Most local health departments serve fewer than 50,000 people.

8
00:00:25,453 --> 00:00:29,833
Small teams. Big questions. Every number has to hold up.

9
00:00:31,393 --> 00:00:35,533
CB-CAP. Know where care breaks. Show the proof.

10
00:00:37,253 --> 00:00:40,913
See where residents drop off, between referral and care.

11
00:00:42,733 --> 00:00:46,713
See which barriers stop them, by kind of help and neighborhood.

12
00:00:49,173 --> 00:00:52,673
Small counts stay hidden, so no one can be identified.

13
00:00:54,533 --> 00:00:58,353
Every number shows its source, its year, and its range.

14
00:00:59,973 --> 00:01:04,593
Your plan becomes your yearly report. People approve every word.

15
00:01:05,813 --> 00:01:08,753
So you walk into the budget meeting with proof.

16
00:01:09,693 --> 00:01:13,873
Bring CB-CAP to your county. Talk to the SozoRock Foundation.

17
00:01:14,613 --> 00:01:17,073
Care. For every zip code.
